---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe11.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Equity-Settled Share-based Payment" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Cash-Settled Share-based Payment" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Vesting Conditions — Service and Performance" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Modifications and Cancellations" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Worked Example — Expensing an Equity-Settled Grant" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — Remeasuring a Cash-Settled Award" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Relationship to IFRS 2" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A genuinely thoroughly converged standard</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 11 governs TRANSACTIONS in WHICH an ENTERPRISE grants EQUITY instruments, or INCURS a LIABILITY based on EQUITY instrument VALUES, as CONSIDERATION for EMPLOYEE services or OTHER goods/SERVICES received. This STANDARD is ONE of the MOST thoroughly CONVERGED within the ENTIRE ASBE suite, CLOSELY mirroring IFRS 2's OWN equity-settled/cash-SETTLED dichotomy internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Equity-settled and cash-settled arrangements</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to SHARE-based PAYMENT transactions with EMPLOYEES (STOCK options, RESTRICTED shares) and, LESS commonly, with OTHER parties PROVIDING goods or SERVICES in EXCHANGE for EQUITY instruments or CASH amounts BASED on the enterprise's SHARE price.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Equity-Settled Share-based Payment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Fair value at grant date, expensed over the vesting period</div><div class="text-supporting">EQUITY-SETTLED share-BASED payment TRANSACTIONS are MEASURED at the FAIR VALUE of the EQUITY instruments GRANTED, DETERMINED at the GRANT date — RECOGNISED as an EXPENSE (WITH a CORRESPONDING increase in CAPITAL RESERVE, WITHIN owners' EQUITY) over the VESTING period, WITHOUT subsequent REMEASUREMENT for changes in FAIR value AFTER the grant DATE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Cash-Settled Share-based Payment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">A liability, remeasured at each reporting date</div><div class="text-supporting">CASH-SETTLED share-BASED payment TRANSACTIONS (e.g. SHARE APPRECIATION rights) are MEASURED at the FAIR VALUE of the LIABILITY incurred — RECOGNISED as an EXPENSE and a CORRESPONDING LIABILITY, WITH the LIABILITY REMEASURED at FAIR value at EACH reporting DATE UNTIL settlement, WITH changes in FAIR value RECOGNISED in PROFIT or LOSS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Vesting Conditions — Service and Performance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Adjusting the expense for the probability of vesting</div><div class="text-supporting">SERVICE CONDITIONS (a REQUIRED period of CONTINUED employment) and PERFORMANCE CONDITIONS (a SPECIFIED performance TARGET) are BOTH reflected by ADJUSTING the NUMBER of equity INSTRUMENTS expected to VEST, RATHER than adjusting the FAIR VALUE per INSTRUMENT itself — CONSISTENT with IFRS 2's OWN treatment internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Modifications and Cancellations</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A minimum expense floor, with incremental value for beneficial modifications</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE an AWARD is MODIFIED in a WAY that INCREASES its FAIR value, the INCREMENTAL fair VALUE is RECOGNISED as an ADDITIONAL expense OVER the REMAINING vesting PERIOD. AT MINIMUM, the ORIGINAL grant-date fair VALUE continues to be RECOGNISED as IF the MODIFICATION had NOT occurred — CONSISTENT with IFRS 2's OWN modification framework.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — Expensing an Equity-Settled Grant</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Spreading grant-date fair value over the vesting period</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A 3-year vesting stock option grant</div><div class="wk-body">A company grants stock options to employees with a total grant-date fair value of RMB 18,000,000, vesting evenly over 3 years of continued service.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises an EXPENSE of RMB 18,000,000 ÷ 3 = <strong>RMB 6,000,000 per year</strong>, with a CORRESPONDING increase in CAPITAL RESERVE within owners' EQUITY, WITHOUT any subsequent REMEASUREMENT for share PRICE movements after the GRANT date.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Remeasuring a Cash-Settled Award</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A liability that moves with the share price</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Share appreciation rights</div><div class="wk-body">A company grants share appreciation rights with a fair value of RMB 4,000,000 at the prior reporting date. By the current reporting date, the fair value of the liability has increased to RMB 5,200,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company RECOGNISES an ADDITIONAL expense of RMB 5,200,000 − RMB 4,000,000 = <strong>RMB 1,200,000</strong>, INCREASING the LIABILITY to RMB 5,200,000 — REFLECTING the ONGOING remeasurement REQUIRED for cash-SETTLED awards, UNLIKE the equity-SETTLED treatment.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 11 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature and terms of share-based payment arrangements</span><span>Methods used to estimate fair value, and the key assumptions applied</span><span>Total expense recognised for equity-settled and cash-settled arrangements separately</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Classifying an arrangement as equity-settled or cash-settled</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Option-pricing model inputs (volatility, expected life, risk-free rate) underlying grant-date fair value</span><span>Expected achievement of performance conditions, and expected forfeiture rates</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 2</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 11 vs IFRS 2</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 11</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 2</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Equity-settled measurement</span><span>Grant-date fair value, no remeasurement</span><span>Grant-date fair value, no remeasurement — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Cash-settled measurement</span><span>Remeasured to fair value each period</span><span>Remeasured to fair value each period — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY closely converged STANDARD — THIS is one of the FEW ASBE topics WHERE the international COMPARISON section HAS very little SUBSTANTIVE divergence to REPORT.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every share-based payment event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Equity-settled expense</span><span><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Credited to capital reserve within equity</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Cash-settled expense</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised as a liability, remeasured each period</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 9</span><span>Employee Benefits — the general employee compensation framework this Standard supplements for equity-based arrangements</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Equity-settled share-based payment</div><div class="glossary-def">A transaction settled by issuing equity instruments, measured at grant-date fair value with no subsequent remeasurement.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Cash-settled share-based payment</div><div class="glossary-def">A transaction settled in cash based on the enterprise's share price, recognised as a liability remeasured to fair value each period.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe11 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
